<h1>Token exchange sample</h1>

<p>
    This project is a Blazor WebAssembly application configured in "interactiveAuto" mode that demonstrates a token exchange 
    sample using OpenIddict. It shows how a Blazor client can authenticate the user and securely exchange access tokens with 
    an OpenID Connect provider.
</p>

<p>
    The sample includes the following features:
    <ul>
        <li>User authentication using OpenID Connect.</li>
        <li>Secure token exchange to obtain access tokens for API calls.</li>
        <li>Integration with an OpenID Connect provider for authentication and token management.</li>
    </ul>   
</p>

<p>
    Two sample users are pre-registered for testing: <b>admin@contoso.com</b> (password: <b>Admin@12345</b>) 
    and <b>user@contoso.com</b> (password: <b>User@12345</b>). 
    The admin user is assigned the <b>Admin</b> role. 
    You can use these credentials to try authentication and token exchange flows in this sample.
</p>